Portability fixes for mo_yanxi_utility, applied by build.mcpp.

Reached as a nested submodule of mo_yanxi_vulkan_wrapper. Upstream is
Yuria-Shikibe/mo_yanxi_utility and this belongs there.

tile.ixx -- `const_iterator = std::const_iterator<tile_iterator>` and the
reverse_iterator over it are guarded on __cpp_lib_ranges_as_const. P2278 is not
in libc++, so the class did not compile there. They are guarded rather than
reimplemented because nothing in this submodule and nothing in xrgui names
either alias, so a local basic_const_iterator would be iterator boilerplate with
no caller.

Everything else routes standard-but-unshipped facilities through the
mo_yanxi.views / mo_yanxi.functional shims that mcpp/mo_yanxi_utility adds
beside this package's manifest:

  tile.ixx                        views::stride, views::slide
  latest/, legacy/, utility/math  std::move_only_function
  interpolation.ixx               range_const_reference_t

Those files are correct standard C++; libc++ has not caught up. Each reverts to
`std::` on its own the day the #if in the shim stops choosing the fallback --
no edit here is needed for that.

